## Feature #5 Increment 1 (spec §4.5) — `for_each` PUMPS the scheduler on
## Pending (not a bare yield), so a TASK-BACKED stream source makes progress.
##
## `QueueStream` is a source whose `poll_next` pulls from an async `Queue`: each
## poll drives one recv step — Ready(value) → `Some(v)`; Pending → the recv
## parked, so the stream is Pending too. It yields EXACTLY ONE element then ends
## (`nil`) — a `want` flag, so we don't depend on queue-close to terminate (an
## end-via-sender-drop would need the producer's `tx` to drop, which params
## don't auto-do — the Feature #4 limit). The element 42 only arrives after the
## SPAWNED producer RUNS — which only happens if `for_each` PUMPS the
## thread-local scheduler on Pending (via `Scope.pump_or_park`). A bare
## `Thread.yield_now` would `sched_yield` forever without pumping the producer →
## spin (Codex high finding). Completing within the harness wall-clock cap,
## having seen 42, proves the pump-on-Pending progress rule.
##
## (Producer is single-send: a spawned multi-await task doesn't self-reschedule
## — the Feature #4 limit; one send is all we need here.)

use std.future.AsyncSender
use std.future.AsyncReceiver

## A Stream over an AsyncReceiver. `poll_next` drives one recv poll.
class QueueStream
  rx_ptr: Int
  remaining: Int
  include Stream
  type Item = Int

  def init(rx_ptr: Int, want: Int)
    self.rx_ptr = rx_ptr
    self.remaining = want
  end

  def var poll_next(cx: &var Context) -> Poll[Option[Int]]
    if self.remaining <= 0
      return Poll.Ready(nil)
    end
    let code = ruxen_queue_recv_step(self.rx_ptr, cx)
    if code == 0
      return Poll.Pending
    end
    if code == 2
      self.remaining = 0
      return Poll.Ready(nil)
    end
    let v = ruxen_queue_recv_taken_value(self.rx_ptr)
    self.remaining = self.remaining - 1
    Poll.Ready(Some(v))
  end
end

async def producer_one(tx: AsyncSender) -> Int
  let _a = tx.send(42).await
  0
end

def main
  puts "stream start"
  let qp = ruxen_queue_new(2, Overflow.Suspend)
  let tx = AsyncSender.new(qp)
  let _h = Task.spawn_raw(producer_one(tx))
  var s = QueueStream.new(qp, 1)
  s.for_each do |v|
    puts "got #{v}"
  end
  puts "stream done"
end
